{
  "name": "decision-journal-system",
  "description": "Build and maintain a decision journal that tracks predictions against outcomes over time. For every significant decision, log the reasoning, the confidence, and the expected outcome before the decision plays out. Review quarterly to compare predictions to actuals. Over time, the journal reveals your systematic biases: where you are consistently overconfident, what types of decisions you get wrong, and where your intuition outperforms your analysis.",
  "steps": [
